<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Benazir Bhutto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1953">1953</a>–<a href="/years/2007">2007</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Benazir Bhutto was a Pakistani politician, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulfikar-ali-bhutto">Zulfikar Ali Bhutto</a> and leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> Peoples Party. She served as prime minister from 1988 to 1990 and from 1993 to 1996, the first woman to lead the government of a Muslim-majority country. Both governments were dismissed amid corruption charges. She was assassinated in Rawalpindi in December 2007 while campaigning after years of exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/benazir-bhutto.jpg" alt="Benazir Bhutto" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oliver_Mark_-_Benazir_Bhutto,_Dubai_2006_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
